ibutes its products through sales force, sales representatives, and digital marketing programs. Genworth Financial, Inc. was founded in 1871 and is headquartered in Glen Allen, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Darren W. Woodell | VP & Controller | Age 49","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $2.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Genworth Financial Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.9B market cap on $7.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 86% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8610395803528854},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2977956.82},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 32% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to GNW Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/38/Technical_Reactions_to_GNW_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111926033401_1795077241.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795077241.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Comparison: Primerica (NYSE:PRI) and Genworth Financial (NYSE:GNW)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/financial-comparison-primerica-nysepri-and-genworth-financial-nysegnw.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794842126.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Inves